  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Yardenone may be associated with ME-180 through a series of molecular interactions involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This complex is a target of both Ponfolin and Broussoaurone A, which in turn have ME-180 as their target. Yardenone is directly linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential mechanism by which it could influence ME-180. The scores from the three paths are consistent, with a final score of 0.5283 in two of the paths, suggesting a strong but not absolute relationship. The evidence supports a pathway where Yardenone acts as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn affects ME-180 through its downstream targets. The mechanism is likely related to the role of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex in epigenetic regulation, and the presence of multiple compounds targeting this complex may contribute to the observed relationship. The evidence is consistent but does not exclude the possibility of additional layers of regulation or alternative pathways.",
